 ## Overview
-Multi-Texture Trilinear Estimation is a direct volume ray casting technique that renders scalar field data defined on a 3D rectilinear grid by stacking parallel quads textured with scalar information and compositing them in depth order [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of visualizing space data where grid cells are not uniform cubes by reconstructing scalar values from a Piecewise Rational (PRI) representation using a hybrid interpolation scheme [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from basic 2D texture rendering by substituting standard trilinear interpolation with two bilinear interpolations and one linear interpolation to improve image quality and speed [S2, unofficial], and from [Trilinear Interpolation](1531-trilinear-interpolation.md) by relying on a stack of slices and dependent texturing rather than direct 3D texture mapping or software-based coordinate array interpolation.
