 *   A Piecewise Rational (PRI) representation of the data, stored as two float textures: one for scalar values and one for knot distances [S1, unofficial].
 *   An index texture mapping spatial positions to spline segments [S1, unofficial].
-*   Camera view direction.
+*   Camera view direction [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Outputs:**
-*   Final 2D image with color and opacity values.
+*   Final 2D image with color and opacity values [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-1.  **Index Texture:** 2D texture where each texel corresponds to a pixel on the PRI sampling plane. Dimensions $w \times h$.
-2.  **Knots Texture:** 2D texture storing the linear splines. Each texel (or set of texels) represents a spline segment. The knots within each spline are sorted in depth (z-direction) [S1, unofficial].
-3.  **Slice Geometry:** A stack of parallel quads.
